**Irish History (2 sentences):**

Ireland's history spans from prehistoric settlement around 34,000 years ago through Celtic, Christian, Viking, and Norman periods, followed by over 800 years of English and British political and military involvement beginning with the Norman invasion in 1169. The island was partitioned in 1922, with 26 counties becoming the independent Irish Free State (later the Republic of Ireland) while six northeastern counties remained part of the United Kingdom as Northern Ireland, leading to decades of sectarian conflict known as the Troubles before the 1998 Good Friday Agreement brought relative peace.
